# pware-os line-ending policy — keep this block identical in every checkout.

# Line endings, one rule: LF in the repository *and* in the working copy, on every
# platform (the box, CI, Linux, the Windows laptops).
#
# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half. With `text=auto` alone, `core.autocrlf=true`
# (the Git-for-Windows default) hands out CRLF, and a file that happens to contain
# a stray CR is classified *binary* by git — after which that path is never
# normalised again, and an edit of ten lines arrives as a whole-file whitespace
# diff. A declared eol removes both halves: nothing is converted on the way out, so
# there is nothing to disagree about.
#
# The two failures this file exists to prevent, both measured on this box: a shell
# script checked out with CRLF makes `#!/usr/bin/env bash` read as `bash\r` and the
# kernel answers "bad interpreter", and `gofmt -l` calls every `.go` file
# unformatted because of the CR it did not write.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The extensions this repo owns are named explicitly rather than left to `auto`: an
# explicit `text` keeps normalising a file even after a stray CR gets into it.
*.go text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# What must keep the bytes it was written with: `cmd.exe` reads a `.bat` poorly
# without CRLF, so those are the one exception, and a repo's own `-text` rules for
# a verbatim pin or a binary stay below this block untouched.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# --- the repo's own rules, kept as they were ---
# Except the pins. These are read by tools that compare them as strings —
# bazelisk parses `.bazelversion` to decide which Bazel to download, a mediapipe
# `.bazelrc` line is read by bazel before any of our code runs, and a stray CR
# turns "7.4.1" into "latest" (which is exactly how six CI runs died: bazel 9
# has WORKSPACE off, and mediapipe's @flatbuffers lives in the WORKSPACE).
.bazelversion text eol=lf
*.bazelrc      text eol=lf
